# Cloudflare serves static assets before the Worker runs, so `headers()` in
# next.config.ts never sees them. The arena's model worker and the ONNX Runtime
# WASM ship as content-hashed /assets/* files, and a dedicated worker spawned
# from a cross-origin-isolated document must carry COEP on its own script
# response — so the isolation headers have to be declared here as well.
#
# Every matching rule is merged, so the isolation headers belong under /* only.
# Repeating them under /assets/* emits each header twice, which parses as
# "same-origin, same-origin" — not a valid token — and the browser falls back
# to unsafe-none, silently losing isolation.
#
# vinext generates this file only when it is absent, so the immutable-cache
# rule it would otherwise write is reproduced below.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Cache content-hashed assets immutably (mirrors vinext's generated default)
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
